From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Platform/Spacemit/K3: \_SB platform _OSC; _LPI removed pending OpenSBI retentive fix

Platform/Spacemit/K3: \_SB platform _OSC; _LPI removed pending OpenSBI retentive fix

Add the \\_SB platform-wide _OSC (UUID 0811B06E-...) confirming
PCLPI (0x80) ONLY: acpi_processor_get_lpi_info() gates _LPI parsing
on osc_pc_lpi_support_confirmed, set exclusively by this handshake
(proven live: 'platform _OSC: OS control mask [00000080]'). The
buffer is 2 DWORDs (u32 capbuf[2]: Query/Status, Support - NO
Control DWORD; a CDW3 at offset 8 would raise AE_AML_BUFFER_LIMIT).
Revision != 1 returns _OSC_REVISION_ERROR (0x08); unknown UUIDs
return _OSC_UNRECOGNIZED_UUID (0x04, not the query bit). PR3/S3,
GED, hotplug-OST not confirmed. (PCI0's _OSC keeps CDW3: pci_root.c
passes capbuf[5].)

REMOVE _LPI from this cycle. The deployed OpenSBI's
__rpmi_hsm_suspend() has NO genuinely retentive path: only sbi
param 0x90000000 takes the per-CPU power-down branch, and EVERY
other value - including SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_RET_DEFAULT (type 0), what
a "retentive WFI" state would request - takes the CLUSTER power-down
vote + D-cache disable + L2 snoop clear before WFI (k3_corepm.c
dispatch). The rpmi-hsm device never returns SBI_ENOTSUPP, so the
kernel-facing sbi_hsm_hart_suspend() plain-wfi fallback is
unreachable on this platform. Consequently NO _LPI state is safely
expressible against this firmware: CPU_NR (0x90000000) hangs the
boot without the kernel's arch_get_idle_state_flags override (tick
broadcast), and a type-0 "SBI_WFI" state is actually a cluster
power-down, not a WFI.

Cpu.asl retains the LPI_STATES macro neutralized (empty) with the
full rationale and the restoration prerequisites in comments.

RESTORATION PREREQUISITES (firmware + kernel, not AML):
1. OpenSBI: implement a genuine retentive default - type 0 as plain
   wfi() with no vote/cache/snoop operations
   (patches/opensbi/0001-k3_corepm-retentive-default-suspend.patch;
   build-verified by disassembly, hardware qualification pending:
   type-0 has no side effects, non-retentive types unchanged,
   timer/IPI/UART wake)
2. Kernel: arch_get_idle_state_flags RISC-V override for timer-stop
3. Then: WFI at index 0 + the qualified suspend state at index 1

Validation: full RELEASE build; built DSDT decodes ZERO _LPI (no
WFI/SBI_WFI/CPU_NR strings) with the \\_SB _OSC present (PCLPI,
2-DWORD contract, revision/UUID error paths). The _OSC handshake is
retained deliberately: it is harmless without _LPI and its live
proof carries to the restoration cycle.
